    26	 * takes the sheet's entry date, its today when off), each a DRAFT claim for the person on the sheet with
    27	 * the name or an alias (ignoring case), added in order. A note ending in " #<reference>" gives the claim that external
    28	 * reference, which is not part of the note. Blank lines are skipped. One change: every line is checked
    29	 * with the claim form's rules (a reference used twice in the paste too, ignoring case), and a refused line
    30	 * refuses the paste, adding nothing and writing nothing.
    31	 * <p>
    32	 * Each line's claim is then opened by the user as the open button would, in paste order; any refusal the
    33	 * open would give refuses the whole paste. A line naming a person, date and note matching one of their
    34	 * claims as they stood before the paste (void and deleted ones aside) updates that claim instead: the
    35	 * newest matching DRAFT takes the line's amount and is opened; matches with no DRAFT refuse the paste.
